<BaseLayout title="How Does It Work?" description="How RisaleTedris helps mixed-age classes study one Risale-i Nur lesson with material suited to each learner." locale="en">
  <section class="page-band"><div class="page-band__inner"><header class="page-title"><p class="eyebrow">How it works</p><h1>One lesson, materials for every age group</h1><p class="lede">RisaleTedris makes it practical for learners of different ages to study the same Risale-i Nur passage together.</p></header></div></section>
  <section class="page-band"><div class="page-band__inner prose-content">
    <h2>The challenge</h2><p>Mixed-age classes need more than one explanation. Learners can study the same text while using questions and activities suited to their own level.</p>
    <h2>The system</h2><p>Each Risale is divided into lesson-sized parts. Every part has grade-specific question sheets, answer material, and flashcards that are ready to use and can be adapted for the class.</p>
    <h2>In the classroom</h2><ol><li>Choose the part to study.</li><li>Give each learner the material for their school range.</li><li>Use flashcards for preparation or memorisation.</li><li>Continue with question sheets while learners read and reflect on the passage.</li><li>Use the answer material to guide discussion and review.</li></ol>
    <h2>Why the questions matter</h2><p>The questions are tied to the particular passage. They encourage reading, understanding, and reflection rather than reliance on general knowledge. Different sets also make individual support easier.</p>
    <h2>One shared lesson, differentiated work</h2><p>The class stays together around one text while each learner works at an appropriate level. This reduces repeated preparation and lets every age group participate meaningfully.</p>
    <h2>Building lasting learning</h2><p>Teachers can review the material with the question bank and flashcards, and select questions from parts already studied for their own final review or assessment.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
